-- title:
--   Isomorphic rigidified fake elliptic curves differ by Γₜ
-- statement:
--   Throughout, all schemes live over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and compositions are written in diagrammatic order.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a positive integer $N$ with $\bar r\neq r$, $r\nmid N$, $\bar r\nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree.
--
--   **Base rings.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. Further, an $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ which is a characteristic-zero domain, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\ (\mathrm{mod}\ \pi)$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally a monoid homomorphism $vdet\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (target written multiplicatively) characterised by $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion data and moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$ and, for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$, the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, a point map `pt` on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli` (isomorphism invariance, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ with $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` on curves with full level-$n$ structure and `hM : IsFineModuli`; a group $G$ with a homomorphism $\rho$ to $\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (the automorphisms lie over the base, they realise the twists by $\chi(g)$ of full level structures, and the labels are multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over the base, invariant under $\rho$, and compatible with the two point maps (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner data.** For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map on curves carrying an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup and `h𝒴 : IsCoarseModuliT`, together with two degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell)\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base, the first forgetting the extra level and the second sending a point to the target of a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`); morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over the base inducing on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion data.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`, i.e. $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the place above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, a finite-adelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is an Eichler order of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$; a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma_t\le\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ is characterised by $\Gamma_t=$ `awayUnits R₁ v`, the units which are local units of $R_1$ at every place other than $v$ (`hΓt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s_\ell\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ with: the local component of $sf_\ell$ equals $s_\ell$ away from $r$ and is $1$ at $r$; the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$ (`hs`); the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w)=\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Special fibre data.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{r^2}\times\mathbb Z_{r^2}$ with `hcoord : IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, the twisted multiplication rule, injective, dense, and the trace rule). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over the same ring (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ in two variables, and `hA₀` saying $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$ and $\theta_0$. Endomorphisms $e(\gamma),e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, lying over the base ($he$), with degrees $\deg(\gamma)$, subject to the clauses: `hE1` ($e(\gamma),e'(\gamma)$ form an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (scalars $\gamma$ act by scalars up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e(\gamma)$ becomes a scalar up to powers of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi_{X_0}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e(\gamma)$ is realised on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (labels in $\Lambda$ describing the effect of $e(\gamma)$ on a full level-$n$ structure, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$), and `hE4` (exhaustion: over any algebraically closed $Onr/(\pi)$-algebra, every $r$-power isogeny pair of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ which preserves the level agrees, up to powers of $r$, with some $e(\gamma)$). A further order-type ring $R_2\le R_1$ with `hR₂o`, whose elements absorb $R_1$ after multiplication by powers of $r$ (`hR₂r`), carrying endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ over the base subject to the clauses `hE5a`–`hE5e` (additivity, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action and preservation of level; unitality and multiplicativity; integers acting through the $\Lambda$-action; the norm relation $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)=\mathrm{nrd}(x)$; compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$; and a joint matrix realisation of $e$ and $\hat e$).
--
--   **Drinfeld moduli data.** A ring homomorphism $\iota\colon\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ and has height $4$; a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf; a classifying map $\eta$ from rigidified objects $\mathrm{Rigidified}\ r\ \Phi\ B$ to $MD$-points, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible objects $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every $MD$-point is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$); an injective homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image has bounded denominators in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). A comparison $eD$ between the functor of $MD$-points with leg and the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$ of Deligne data for $(K_0,\pi)$, together with the clauses `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (it preserves the leg), `hGLD` (it converts the $MD$-action by $g$ into the $vdet$-twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of $g$), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` (it converts $\pi$-translation into a Frobenius twist of the leg, and $\pi$-translates exist). A homomorphism $\kappa$ from $Onr/(\pi)$ to $Onr/(r)$ lifting the two quotient maps, an integer $n_0$ and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner data on the special fibre.** A curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/(\pi)$ with morphisms $aw,aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), an exponent $k_w$ and morphisms $bw,bw'$ forming an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, the joint matrix realisation in which the $e(\gamma)$ correspond to $g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ and $aw$ followed by $bw$ corresponds to $g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$, both up to powers of $r$.
--
--   **The classifying map on rigidified curves.** A map $\Xi$ assigning to a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a leg $\psi\colon Onr\to B$ and a rigidified curve in $\mathrm{RigidifiedCurve}\ r\ \pi\ A_0\ B\ \psi$ — that is, a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a rigidification consisting of a curve $E_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ pulled back from $E$, a curve $A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ pulled back from $A_0$ along the residue of $\psi$, and an $r^{d}$-isogeny pair $\varphi,\varphi'$ between $E_b$ and $A_b$ preserving the level — a $GPoint$ of $MD$, subject to: `hΞleg` (over a connected base the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under an isomorphism of curves which is compatible with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level, and which is matched by comparison data between the rigidifications up to powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (the explicit description of $\Xi$: for a connected base with $r$ nilpotent and a formal module structure on the curve there are $j\le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with the same formal module, transported from $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, such that $\Xi$ equals the point with leg $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$ and class $\eta(t)$).
--
--   **The fixed matrix and the comparison clauses.** A matrix $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, with `heqΓ` and `heqW`: over a connected base, an $e(\gamma)$-translate of a rigidification, respectively a rigidification matched with an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ through $aw$ followed by $bw$, corresponds under $\Xi$ to the $MD$-action by $r^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1})$, respectively by $r^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1})$, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$. The clauses `hK1`–`hK4` describe the fibre over one leg: existence of a rigidified curve with prescribed image $(\psi,P)$ under $eD\circ\Xi$ twisted by $g_0^{-1}$; uniqueness of such a curve up to an isomorphism with comparison data; compatibility with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; and lifting along a surjection whose kernel has square zero. The clauses `hC0e`, `hC0u` give existence and uniqueness of a normalised level-$n$ transport `IsNormLevelTransport` of $P_0$ along a rigidification. A map $\Theta_f$ from the product of the corepresentable functor of $Onr$, the functor $\Omega$ and the constant functor $G$ to the nilpotent points of $M$, with `hnat` (naturality), `hG` ($G$-equivariance), `hC2` (its first component is the $M$-point of the curve with its transported level-$n$ structure) and `hC2c` (composing with $p$ gives the $\mathcal X$-point of the curve). A group homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\Gamma_t\to G$ and the clause `hC3`, which states that a $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted translate of $(\psi,P)$ is realised by another rigidification of the same curve with the same image, whose level-$n$ transport is the $\chi(\theta_t(\gamma))$-twist of the original one, and whose extra level-$\ell$ subgroups, for primes $\ell\neq r$ invertible on the base, are detected by the same points.
--
--   **Hypotheses over $k$.** An algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent in it, a leg $\psi\colon Onr\to k$, two Deligne data $P,P'\in\Omega(k)$, two fake elliptic curves $E,E'$ over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho,\varrho'$ relative to the twisted leg $\psi\circ Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}$, such that each of the two $\Xi$-points $\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ and $\langle E',\varrho'\rangle$ has leg equal to that twisted leg (`hΞψ`, `hΞψ'`) and its image under $eD$ is carried by the $vdet$-twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ to $(\psi,P)$, respectively $(\psi,P')$ (`hev`, `hev'`); and an isomorphism $i\colon E.A\cong E'.A$ with $i$ over the base ($hi$) which satisfies `IsoVia`, i.e. it is compatible with the two group laws, commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions, and a point factors through the level-$N$ structure of $E$ exactly when its image factors through that of $E'$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist $\gamma\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and a proof that $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ such that:
--
--   (i) $(\psi,P')$ is the $vdet$-twisted translate of $(\psi,P)$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$, that is `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet k (Units.map ι₀ γ) (ψ, P) (ψ, P')`: the leg is unchanged, $\psi=\psi\circ Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0(\gamma))}$, and for every full lattice $M$ the line of $P'$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed action of $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$; and
--
--   (ii) there is a further rigidification $\varrho''$ of the same curve $E$ relative to the same twisted leg for which
--
--   (a) the $\Xi$-point of $\langle E,\varrho''\rangle$ has leg equal to the twisted leg, and its image under $eD$ is carried by the $vdet$-twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ to $(\psi,P')$;
--
--   (b) $\varrho''$ is the $e(\gamma)$-translate of $\varrho$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.IsTranslateBy hΛℤ`: there are morphisms $u\colon\varrho''.E_b.A\to\varrho.E_b.A$ and $u_A\colon\varrho''.A_b.A\to\varrho.A_b.A$ exhibiting the two reductions as pullbacks along the identity and compatible with $g_b$ and $g_A$, together with an endomorphism $e_{\gamma b}$ of $\varrho.A_b.A$ over the base lifting $e(\gamma)$ through $\varrho.g_A$ and natural numbers $i,j$ such that $u$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$, then $e_{\gamma b}$, then multiplication by $r^{i}$ equals $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by $u_A$ and multiplication by $r^{j}$; and
--
--   (c) $\varrho''$ corresponds to $\varrho'$ along $i$: there exist a morphism $ib\colon\varrho''.E_b.A\to\varrho'.E_b.A$ with $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\varrho''.g_b$ followed by $i$, and $ib$ lying over the base, a morphism $u_A\colon\varrho'.A_b.A\to\varrho''.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as a pullback of $\varrho''.A_b$ along the identity and satisfying $u_A$ followed by $\varrho''.g_A$ equal to $\varrho'.g_A$, and natural numbers $i_1,j_1$ such that $ib$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, then $u_A$, then multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ on $\varrho''.A_b$ equals $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   This is the transport step at the heart of the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the fibre of the rigidified family over a single leg: it shows that an isomorphism between two rigidified fake elliptic curves over an algebraically closed base with $\pi$ nilpotent is induced by an element of the arithmetic group $\Gamma_t$, which then acts on Drinfeld's Deligne data by the $vdet$-twisted action through $\iota_0$. It is used by the companion statement that adds the level-$N$ and extra-level clauses to this correspondence.
